// OpenRC Simulator - Glider 2400
//
// Two-and-a-half metre thermal glider.
// Very low wing loading, a long slender wing and a high-lift section: it climbs in air a powered model would not notice and takes an age to come down.
// The motor is there to get it up, not to fly it.
// Rudder does most of the turning - the ailerons are small and the adverse yaw is real.
//
// Units are SI throughout, body axes are FRD (x nose, y right wing, z down),
// and the layout mirrors Trainer1500.json - four wing panels a side, so the
// spanwise resolution of the aerodynamics is the same across the roster.
//
// validation_targets are MEASURED, not asserted: scripts/measure-aircraft.sh
// flies the aeroplane and fills them in. Until then this block is empty and
// the regression suite checks only that the airframe is physically coherent.
